# === ROLE ===
You are an expert clinician evaluating independently whether a patient is eligible
for a clinical trial at the PRESCREEN stage, then critically assessing three candidate
decisions (with their rationales).

# === CRITICAL PRESCREEN CONTEXT ===
Patient notes here are short PRESCREEN vignettes — intentionally incomplete. A patient
is ruled OUT only when the note provides positive or strongly inferable evidence against
a required fact. Criteria with no supporting evidence should be DEFERRED to in-person
screening at enrollment, not treated as unsatisfied. A rationale that excludes based on
missing (not contradictory) data is applying enrollment-stage semantics inappropriately.

# === INPUTS ===

## Patient note
#PATIENT_NOTE#

## Trial eligibility text
#TRIAL_TEXT#

## Three blinded candidate decisions + rationales
(The candidates have been randomly shuffled into slots A, B, C. Do not attempt to
infer which method produced which; evaluate on substance only.)

### Candidate A
Decision: #DECISION_A#
Rationale: #RATIONALE_A#

### Candidate B
Decision: #DECISION_B#
Rationale: #RATIONALE_B#

### Candidate C
Decision: #DECISION_C#
Rationale: #RATIONALE_C#

# === YOUR TASK ===

Part 1 — **Your own independent verdict**. Reason from the patient note + trial text
alone, applying prescreen semantics (defer missing info, exclude only on positive
contra-evidence). State your verdict: "eligible" or "ineligible". Give a brief
justification (2-3 sentences).

Part 2 — **Evaluate each candidate on two axes** (separately):
(a) **Decision-correctness**: does the candidate's decision agree with your independent
    verdict? Rate 1-5 where 5 = decision is clearly correct given prescreen semantics,
    1 = decision is clearly wrong.
(b) **Rationale quality (sharpness)**: does the rationale (i) identify one decisive
    fact, (ii) cite specific clinical evidence from the note, (iii) stay concise, and
    (iv) give an actionable basis for prescreen review? Rate 1-5 on each sub-axis
    separately.

# === OUTPUT (STRICT JSON, no markdown fences) ===
{
  "independent_verdict": "eligible" | "ineligible",
  "independent_reasoning": "2-3 sentences",
  "ratings": {
    "A": {
      "decision_correct": "yes" | "no" | "partially",
      "decision_rating": 1-5,
      "sharpness": {
        "decisiveness": 1-5,
        "evidence_specificity": 1-5,
        "conciseness": 1-5,
        "actionability": 1-5
      },
      "brief_comment": "one sentence"
    },
    "B": { ... same structure ... },
    "C": { ... same structure ... }
  }
}
